    "created_at": "2020-03-03T00:35:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-03-03T00:35:44Z",
    "body": "Yes, Firefox will report parse/evaluation errors.  (SharedWorkers' handling I believe lives [here](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/91f6c02fcf4c16f78fdc4417f61f192688294066/dom/workers/WorkerError.cpp#73) which has special cases for each of the 3 types of workers).  And it seems appropriate for this to be in the spec.\r\n\r\nHowever, it looks like Blink doesn't report the error?  I made a quick test case at https://worker-playground.glitch.me/shared-worker-top-level-error.html that does console.log() for Dedicated and Shared Workers on the same file, and Firefox reports both errors, but Chrome does not.  (And Safari doesn't support SharedWorkers.)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
