    "created_at": "2020-03-03T12:06:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-03-03T12:06:18Z",
    "body": "Yes, the spec should be changed.  And in the case of multiple SharedWorker instances, it would seem to make sense that every `SharedWorker` instance associated with the given `worker global scope` be notified of the error.  If there's only one `SharedWorker` at the time of evaluation, only one hears about it.\r\n\r\nI wonder if this should be handled by changing https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#runtime-script-errors-2 to treat shared workers similarly to dedicated workers?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
