    "created_at": "2020-03-03T12:57:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-03-03T12:57:19Z",
    "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#runtime-script-errors-2 basically describes bubbling an error event from [WorkerGlobalScope, Worker, Worker's global scope] (unless handled).  If the SharedWorker's global doesn't handle the error due to breakage, why wouldn't content want to be able to know that?  A lot of recent discussion in the ServiceWorker WG relates to sites being paranoid about ServiceWorker and storage breakage, so providing a mechanism to detect unhandled errors seems useful, if duplicative.\r\n\r\nCoincidentally, Firefox also reports runtime errors.  I created https://worker-playground.glitch.me/shared-worker-dynamic-error.html which logs both errors from `onconnect` and `onmessage` from a handler added in `onconnect`.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
